  "source": {
    "answer": "1",
    "level": 2,
    "problem": "Let $\\omega$ be a complex number such that $\\omega^3 = 1.$  Find all possible values of\n\\[\\frac{1}{1 + \\omega} + \\frac{1}{1 + \\omega^2}.\\]Enter all the possible values, separated by commas.",
    "solution": "We can write\n\\begin{align*}\n\\frac{1}{1 + \\omega} + \\frac{1}{1 + \\omega^2} &= \\frac{1 + \\omega^2 + 1 + \\omega}{(1 + \\omega)(1 + \\omega^2)} \\\\\n&= \\frac{2 + \\omega + \\omega^2}{1 + \\omega + \\omega^2 + \\omega^3} \\\\\n&= \\frac{2 + \\omega + \\omega^2}{2 + \\omega + \\omega^2} \\\\\n&= \\boxed{1}.\n\\end{align*}",
